    "summary": "Cloth, an imported cotton cloth with the same pattern as Af1981,11.3. This has been adapted by the Kalabari by cutting out sections (in the process called ‘pelete bite’) of the white, yellow, red and blue warp threads to create three patterns named “Glass Tail”, “Kiene Uncut”, and “Sangolo.” The cloth has not been hemmed.",
